arm64: dts: rockchip: add the RK3576 PWM controllers

Nothing described the PWM blocks, so a board could not reach a backlight
or a fan. Add the two general-purpose controllers: pwm1 with six channels
from 0x2add0000 and pwm2 with eight from 0x2ade0000. Each channel is its
own 4 KiB register page and its own device; they share the controller's
functional and APB clocks.

The pinctrl default is the m0 mux for each channel, which a board that
routes a channel elsewhere overrides.

The PMU-domain controller at 0x27330000 is left out - nothing on the
boards to hand uses it, so there is no way to test it.

Signed-off-by: Isaiah DeRose-Wilson <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

